finding: The direct-v0.9.5 migration claim is false: MIGRATION.md:324 lists `/render/core` MeshInstanceInput as a former public import. `git grep 'MeshInstanceInput\|PartInput' v0.9.5 -- packages/shallot/src` returns no matches; this schema never shipped in 0.9.5. The nearby Before/After table likewise lists InstanceInput and PickingIdFn as unchanged old imports, although v0.9.5 has no InstanceInput and used TagFn. Remove intermediate-release-only rows and use the actual stable names (with the existing rename mapping where applicable). This is a documentation finding, not a demonstrated rendering regression. Independently ran light-inputs.gpu.test.ts, shadows.gpu.test.ts, material-shadows.node.ts and targets.node.ts; all pass. Re-ran targets against /tmp/shallot-stage10-all-shadows-base: all eight byte comparisons pass. A temporary test (removed afterward) exercised directional/point shadowMapsEnabled off/on, two cascades and restoration, standalone spot and point/spot coexistence (one spot combo, spot disabled suppresses point shadows), spot NotShadowCaster add/remove with exact occupied-depth restoration, and PointShadows.casters=1 with two spots. All pass without validation errors. Existing marker test proves unmarked peers still cast. GPU light-input layout and cluster shader math are unchanged; new authoring columns feed the same degree-valued 32-byte input record. Spot precedence is explicitly documented in SpotLight JSDoc. Search found no obsolete mesh/light public exports. Notes: ColorGrading.hue remains radians while spot cones, camera FOV and Euler helpers use degrees. By the stated authored-angle rule hue should also be degrees, but it predates this stage (presentation stage 2), so this is a cross-stage consistency note rather than a stage-10 behavior finding. Bevy light fields and exclusions were compared; retained linear intensity, legacy bias defaults and camera shape are within narrowed scope. Uncertainty: adapter identity unavailable, no hardware qualification; baseline bytes were the supplied saved e550a7b0 fixture, not independently regenerated. Narrow caster-budget run verifies cap enforcement, not exhaustive atlas saturation/hysteresis configurations. No full suite run.
